  "caution_policy": {
    "doc": "Owner ruling 2026-09-27, restated 2026-10-04 11:44: a caution site PREPARES, it does not SWAP. A recorded site never lowers a lift's rank and never takes a main or compound lift off the shortlist (the safety_load grade stays a fact for the split screen, not a ranking penalty). It adds the site's prep drills to every session holding a lift that uses the site (split_model.uses_site), caution drills first, inside the prep budget -- the prep runs before the first lift. The ONLY swaps are `substitutions` (site -> {from: to}, owner-approved rows only): `from` leaves the pool, `to` takes its rank, the plan records replaces/for_site and says it in one summary line; nothing is asked. A lift not in the table keeps its place. `notes` are range/load notes on a kept lift (copy: health.plan.caution_note.<lift>), never swaps; their dose caps stay in knee_precedents.",
